,"hint":"The modifier introduces a **singular count noun phrase**, not just an adjective.","explanation":"Before singular count task with an adjective, use **such a useful task**.","keywords":["such-noun-phrase"],"skill":"such-noun-phrase","contextKey":"degree-comparison-2","fingerprint":"e8eeda580189134694c52b893dbfb0153b866d2e0da46c33d88fad38275fe35e","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-degree"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The modifier introduces a **singular count noun phrase**, not just an adjective.","Before singular count task with an adjective, use **such a useful task**.","Choose **such a**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"So does not take this article + adjective + noun order.","B":"The singular count noun needs the article in this phrase.","C":"The neutral order is such a, not a such.","D":"Before singular count task with an adjective, use **such a useful task**."}}},{"id":"797f2e0d-6aa4-5d2b-a43b-7794dfcd19ed","topicSlug":"degree-comparison","level":"B1","prompt":"Choose the degree modifier that fits: “It is ____ easier to restore the old portrait with help.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"very"},{"id":"B","text":"many"},{"id":"C","text":"such"},{"id":"D","text":"much"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Easier is already **comparative**; choose a modifier that works with comparisons.","explanation":"**Much** can modify comparative easier to show a large difference.","keywords":["comparative-modifier"],"skill":"comparative-modifier","contextKey":"degree-comparison-2","fingerprint":"3c80815690b4ecfb0c84579c55a72d7a26e47d324d74527151fe93a2c36a0708","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-degree"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Easier is already **comparative**; choose a modifier that works with comparisons.","**Much** can modify comparative easier to show a large difference.","Choose **much**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Very does not normally modify a comparative directly.","B":"Many counts plural nouns, not a comparative adjective.","C":"Such normally modifies a noun phrase, not easier by itself.","D":"**Much** can modify comparative easier to show a large difference."}}},{"id":"8df51990-f456-5ebc-a60d-fae09849aba2","topicSlug":"degree-comparison","level":"B1","prompt":"The instructions let us do the task. “They are ____ to help us measure the garden fence.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"enough clear"},{"id":"B","text":"clearly enough"},{"id":"C","text":"enough clearly"},{"id":"D","text":"clear enough"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"Enough follows **adjectives**, but precedes **nouns**.","explanation":"Enough follows the adjective: **clear enough**.","keywords":["enough-adjective-order"],"skill":"enough-adjective-order","contextKey":"degree-comparison-3","fingerprint":"9e1b48892aa71d6cd9f3ce3001024d702dc0a64e47ac83c5d358d0ca1091676d","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-degree"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Enough follows **adjectives**, but precedes **nouns**.","Enough follows the adjective: **clear enough**.","Choose **clear enough**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Enough normally follows an adjective.","B":"The adjective describes the instructions; clearly is an adverb.","C":"This uses an adverb and reverses its normal relation to enough.","D":"Enough follows the adjective: **clear enough**."}}},{"id":"7a85dbc0-4bad-5983-a6b0-cd489491cdb6","topicSlug":"degree-comparison","level":"B1","prompt":"“We have ____ to measure the gar